{
  "id": "2026-10-03-stratego-ai",
  "title": "An AI just beat the best Stratego player ever, and it cost less than a used car",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "This week, an AI beat the best Stratego player who has ever lived.",
    "If you've never played it, Stratego is a bit like chess with the lights off.",
    "Each player sets up forty pieces face down, so you can't see what your opponent has.",
    "You only find out what a piece is when it runs into one of yours.",
    "That makes bluffing part of the game, and it's why computers struggled with it for so long.",
    "The new system is called Ataraxos, and it comes from researchers at Carnegie Mellon, NYU, Stanford, and MIT.",
    "In a twenty-game match, it took on Pim Niemeijer, a Dutch player with four world titles.",
    "It won fifteen games, lost one, and drew four.",
    "The surprising part is the price tag.",
    "A few years ago, Google DeepMind spent millions of dollars on its own Stratego AI and still fell short.",
    "Ataraxos was trained for under eight thousand dollars, on sixteen GPUs, in about a week.",
    "Its trick is to keep guessing what the hidden pieces probably are, and to update those guesses after every move.",
    "The team thinks the same idea could carry over to negotiations, where nobody shows all their cards.",
    "Next time you bluff in a meeting, remember that the machines are getting good at it too.",
    "Try telling someone about this over lunch today. It makes a great conversation starter!"
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "카네기멜런·NYU·스탠퍼드·MIT 연구진의 AI 'Ataraxos' 가 스트라테고 역대 최강자 핌 니에마이어(세계 챔피언 4회)를 20판 중 15승 1패 4무로 꺾었다. 9월 30일 Nature 에 실렸다.",
    "스트라테고는 말 40개를 뒤집어 놓고 시작해 부딪혀야 정체가 드러나는 게임이라, 블러핑이 핵심이고 그래서 AI 가 오래 못 넘던 벽이었다.",
    "놀라운 건 비용이다 — 몇 년 전 딥마인드는 수백만 달러를 쓰고도 못 이겼는데, Ataraxos 는 GPU 16장으로 일주일, 8천 달러 미만에 훈련됐다. 숨은 말의 정체를 계속 추정하고 수마다 고치는 방식이고, 협상처럼 정보가 가려진 영역에도 쓸 수 있다고 본다."
  ],
